{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"like/from"}],"gloss":"like the ocean/wheel"},{"surface":"தோன்றும்","parts":[{"text":"தோன்றும்","lemma":"தோன்று","gloss":"appears"}],"gloss":"appears"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஓர்எயில்","parts":[{"text":"ஓர்","lemma":"ஒன்று","gloss":"one"},{"text":"எயில்","lemma":"எயில்","gloss":"fortress"}],"gloss":"one fortress"},{"surface":"மன்னன்","parts":[{"text":"மன்னன்","lemma":"மன்னன்","gloss":"king"}],"gloss":"king"},{"surface":"ஒரு","parts":[{"text":"ஒரு","lemma":"ஒன்று","gloss":"one"}],"gloss":"one"},{"surface":"மட","parts":[{"text":"மட","lemma":"மடம்","gloss":"innocent/tender"}],"gloss":"innocent/tender"},{"surface":"மகளே","parts":[{"text":"மகள்","lemma":"மகள்","gloss":"daughter"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"daughter indeed"}]}],"literal":"Plough-spread fields, water-spread wet fields / Paddy-abundant houses, gold-abundant streets / Humming bees buzzing in the many-flowered grove / Like Poantai of the great chief Ātaṉ / She is of great fame and rare wealth, black-branched / Neem, mountain ebony, and palmyra, all three / Those with heads wearing them, those with bows bearing them / Even if victorious kings give, according to his own worth / He will not give to those who do not bow, fertile-clustered / In the middle of the intertwined ears of grain paddy field, being protected / Appears like a drying ship in the ocean / The unique daughter of the king of the single-fortress town.","translation":"She is the only, innocent daughter of the king of the single-walled fortress town, which appears like a ship stranded and drying in the middle of the ocean, surrounded by paddy fields with intertwined ears of grain. Her town is of great fame and rare wealth, like Poantai of the great chief Ātaṉ, with plough-spread fields, water-spread wet fields, paddy-abundant houses, gold-abundant streets, and groves of many flowers where humming bees buzz. Even if the victorious kings who wear the three garlands of black-branched neem, mountain ebony, and palmyra, and bear bows, come and offer gifts, her father will not give her hand to those who do not bow to him in respect.","modern":"ஏர்கள் பரவிய வயல்களையும், நீர் நிறைந்த கழனிகளையும், நெல் மலிந்த வீடுகளையும், பொன் மலிந்த தெருக்களையும், வண்டுகள் ஒலிக்கும் பல மலர்கள் நிறைந்த சோலைகளையும் உடைய, நெடுவேள் ஆதனின் போந்தை என்னும் ஊரைப் போன்ற, பெரும் புகழும் அரிய செல்வமும் உடையவள் அவள். கரிய கிளைகளைக் கொண்ட வேம்பு, ஆர், போந்தை ஆகிய மூன்று மாலைகளையும் சூடிய தலைகளையும், விற்களையும் ஏந்திய வெற்றி வேந்தர்கள் வந்து கேட்டாலும், தன் தகுதிக்கு ஏற்பப் பணியாதவர்களுக்கு அவளைத் தரமாட்டான். நெருங்கிய கதிர்களைக் கொண்ட வயல்களின் நடுவே, கடலில் காய்ந்து கிடக்கும் கலம் போலத் தோன்றும் ஒற்றை மதிலைக் கொண்ட ஊரின் மன்னனுடைய ஒப்பற்ற இளமகள் அவள்.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Puram genre, specifically the theme of Makaṭpāṟ Kāñci (the refusal of a daughter's hand in marriage). The poet, Kuṉṟūr Kiḻār Makaṉār, describes the beauty and wealth of the heroine's town, comparing it to the famous town of Poantai belonging to the chief Ātaṉ. The girl's father is a proud chieftain of a small, single-walled fortress town that stands out amidst vast paddy fields like a ship in the ocean. Great kings of the three major dynasties (Cēra, Cōḻa, and Pāṇṭiya, symbolized by their respective garlands of palmyra, mountain ebony, and neem) come with their bows to demand her hand. However, the proud father refuses to give his daughter to anyone who does not bow to him in respect, even if they are mighty monarchs. This highlights the fierce pride and independence of the local chieftains of the classical Tamil land.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}